Powerful moment from Israel’s UN Ambassador Danny Danon: he walked up to the Islamic Republic’s representative at the UN and offered him the Starlink terminal Netanyahu showed in his speech, so the Iranian people can finally access uncensored internet. The official refused. That’s the regime in one clip: they would rather keep their own people in the dark than accept a tool for freedom.
Iranians have been risking their lives for years just to get online. The terror regime shuts down the internet whenever protests begin. Starlink terminals already help some, but Direct-to-Cell changes the game: no special dish is needed, just a regular phone.
@POTUS, sign an executive order that clears the regulatory path for Starlink Direct-to-Cell so it can reach people living under digital dictatorships. @ElonMusk and @SpaceX already built the tech. Let it serve the Iranian people the way it has served Ukrainians and others.
Internet freedom is not a luxury. It is a human right. The Iranian people deserve it.
@NUFDIran @PahlaviComms

